            <ArticleTitle>Chronic abdominal pain and homesickness in an adolescent male.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>338-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Recurrent abdominal pain is a frequent presenting complaint for adolescents under stress. For many, this symptom provides legitimate access to a medical provider, where other, &quot;hidden&quot; psychosocial agendas may be safely explored. However, providers should be cautious and not neglect the physical examination and diagnostic work-up. In this case report, we describe the discovery of underlying parasitic infections in an adolescent with multiple psychosocial stressors and abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
